title: HaroldAudenClue0
---
Harold Auden’s grandfather lived on a few acres of land in the countryside. Poorly maintained, the grass grew tall, nearly the height of 8 year-old Harold. On a visit during the peak of summer, Harold escaped his mother’s eye and ran into the vast field, pretending to be a lion on the hunt for prey. The fantasy withered when his mother yelled his name, and Harold was forced to come sulking back. After an expected finger wagging, his mother began inspecting him head to toe and then suddenly screamed. She jumped back from him, pointing toward a swollen tick feasting on his thin leg. After plucking out the parasite, she dragged him to several doctor’s visits, but no one could ever find the poison she was so certain lurked within him. 
===

title: HaroldAudenClue1
---
WWhile Harold was fascinated by horror stories growing up, nothing stuck with him quite like the story of the Dunwich Horror. A being somewhere between human and cosmic god, the idea of a human-figure hiding his evil nature beneath a human skin disturbed him. Even the thought of it made him feel invisible bugs skittering under the surface of his own skin. He lay awake at night imagining a human face melting into a mess of flesh and tentacles, the Dunwich Horror in its true form.
===

title: HaroldAudenClue2
---
Harold’s school life was stunted before it began. His mother’s compulsive need to control his behavior left him with a crippling fear of interacting with other kids on his own. But at least he had Jacob Allerton. A similarly shy boy, Jacob and Harold didn’t talk much, preferring to simply sit together during class and occasionally exchange glances. One day, Harold’s mother invited Jacob over for a playdate. Their friendship began with an awkward attempt at playing tag and ended with Harold’s blood washing away sidewalk chalk and Jacob being unceremoniously moved to another school, towns away. 
===